=== D. the arity ladder: transitive on pairs, not on triples ===
|G| = 60  (PSL(2,5) = A5 on 6 points)
  orbits on PAIRS   : [15]   transitive: True
  orbits on TRIPLES : [10, 10]   transitive: False
  |T n T'| within A : {1: 60, 2: 30}
  |T n T'| within B : {1: 60, 2: 30}
  |T n T'| A x B    : {0: 10, 1: 30, 2: 60}
  => already separated by the crudest pair invariant a coherent closure has

  2-closure obstruction: a 2-transitive group has only the two orbitals
  {diagonal, rest}, so its 2-closure is the FULL symmetric group.  Hence no
  edge-coloured graph on the cell can have such a group as its automorphisms.
  brute force over all 32768 graphs on 6 vertices: 2-transitive-but-not-S6 automorphism groups found = 0
